---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PersonJsonLd from '../components/PersonJsonLd.astro';
import portrait from '../assets/portrait.jpeg';
---

<Base
  title="About — Arda Başarıcı"
  description="Mathematics → game development → AI engineering, evaluation-first. Building in public."
>
  <PersonJsonLd />
  <article>
    <div class="head">
      <div>
        <h1>About</h1>
        <p class="lede">I enjoy moving between concrete problems and the abstractions that connect them.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="portrait">
        <Image src={portrait} alt="Arda Başarıcı" width={195} densities={[1.5, 2]} quality={85} />
      </div>
    </div>

    <p>
      I'm an AI engineer with a mathematics background. I build LLM systems
      evaluation-first: deterministic where a model isn't needed, measured against
      ground truth where one is, and open about the error that remains. I run two of
      them in public.
      The <a class="qlink" href="https://leave-agent.ardabasarici.dev">Leave Impact Agent</a> reads
      an organization's HR system, issue tracker, calendar and documents, works out what
      a leave affects and drafts a coverage plan for a person to approve; it is graded
      against a synthetic organization generated together with its answer
      key. <a class="qlink" href="https://steamlens.ardabasarici.dev">SteamLens</a> analyzes
      Steam reviews and publishes its evidence, its sampling uncertainty and its measured
      error rates. I built both end to end: the evaluation data, the backend, the spend
      controls and the deployment.
    </p>

    <p>
      Based in Turkey (UTC+3) and currently looking for AI/LLM engineering roles
      involving evaluation, backend integration and deployment: open to remote roles
      (contract or EOR) and to
      relocation. <a class="qlink" href="mailto:ardabasarici@gmail.com">Email</a> is the
      fastest way to reach me;
      the <a class="qlink" href="/resume/Arda_Basarici_Resume.pdf">resume</a> is a PDF.
    </p>

    <h2>How I got here</h2>

    <p>
      I studied mathematics at Boğaziçi University (a B.Sc. followed by graduate
      coursework) and worked as a teaching assistant, leading problem-solving sessions
      across seven undergraduate courses. Mathematics set the standard I still hold work
      to: a claim isn't finished until the reasoning behind it holds.
    </p>

    <p>
      Then came three years as a game developer, building and shipping 20+ production
      games and interactive experiences for platforms like AirConsole, CrazyGames, and
      Snapchat. Games taught the other half of the job: real users, real deadlines, and
      systems judged in production rather than on paper.
    </p>

    <p>
      AI engineering combines the two: production software whose behaviour is an
      empirical question. The field calls that discipline evaluation; it's the part I
      care about most.
    </p>

    <h2>How I work</h2>

    <p>
      What interests me most isn't just finding an answer, but understanding the structure
      underneath it: what assumptions it depends on, what information it preserves, and whether
      the conclusions are actually justified by the evidence. In practice:
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>A number with no baseline and no error bar isn't a result yet.</li>
      <li>A conclusion is earned by the experiment that could have falsified it.</li>
      <li>Negative results are findings, and I publish them as such: the Leave Impact Agent's own report shows a single full-context call scoring higher than it on the smaller corpus, 30 scenarios to 24, beside the agent's 24 to 14 on the larger.</li>
      <li>Published runs carry their seed, config and code version, and the model outputs they used are stored alongside them.</li>
      <li>Complexity must earn its place: no framework or layer that doesn't demonstrably buy something.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      I use Claude Code daily. I work through a system's shape with it and make the
      decisions; it writes much of the code, the tests and the documentation drafts, and a
      change is accepted only after I have reviewed it and tests, CI and expected
      behaviour pass.
    </p>

    <h2>Current areas of focus</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>LLM applications and agent workflows</li>
      <li>Evaluation and experiment design</li>
      <li>Backend integration, deployment and operation</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      Earlier work in reinforcement learning, simulation and data analysis is on the
      projects page.
    </p>

    <p>
      I build in public: <a class="qlink fwd" href="/projects/">projects
      and technical reports</a> here, and posts
      on <a class="qlink" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/ardabasarici">LinkedIn</a> and <a
        class="qlink"
        href="https://x.com/ardabasarici">X</a>, including the mistakes, dead ends, and
      lessons learned.
    </p>

  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .head {
    display: flex;
    gap: 40px;
    align-items: flex-start;
    justify-content: flex-start;
  }
  .head > div:first-child {
    flex: 0 1 auto;
  }
  .portrait {
    flex: 0 0 195px;
    height: 195px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    margin-top: -6px;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    box-shadow: 5px 5px 0 var(--shadow);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .portrait img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: 50% 26%;
    display: block;
  }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .head {
      flex-direction: column-reverse;
    }
    .portrait {
      flex: 0 0 auto;
      width: 120px;
      height: 120px;
    }
  }
  h2 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 23px;
    color: var(--bright);
    margin: 30px 0 10px;
  }
  .lede {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 21px;
    color: var(--amber);
    max-width: 32ch;
  }
  p,
  li {
    max-width: 64ch;
  }
  ul {
    padding-left: 22px;
  }
  li {
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }
</style>
